{"title":"2009 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 50th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 2009 in Bremen, Germany. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1.</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2.</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3.</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4.</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5.</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6.</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1.\">Problem 1.</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1.\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d43f85698b8d1250316b575e6c79c4250708ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,\\ldots,a_k (k\\ge2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> be distinct integers in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5f1c3191725ed0fe5e5809e2e707141b876495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3546ec8332d6784455952774050f4cf5cd2588b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i(a_{i+1}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85f9e32cd8c03d88a00f03b82fa36fa44f07cbe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,\\ldots,k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> doesn't divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c6b53a225bccd0246cf98a5b5bab093dd41005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k(a_1-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>Author: Ross Atkins, Australia</i>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2.\">Problem 2.</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2.\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with circumcentre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are interior points of the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9141cf60419b778a5a3a2d5c6ef4d5e5200ff45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoints of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/666a267ed622c158b00676df18f0fd043c8504e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP,CQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, respectively, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> be the circle passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9141cf60419b778a5a3a2d5c6ef4d5e5200ff45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is tangent to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e6b8eb3853536162118052909c13b675829f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p><i>Author: Sergei Berlov, Russia</i>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3.\">Problem 3.</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3.\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7dd022774271e03b3e6fa8e84093b89e1aec93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1,s_2,s_3,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"11\" /> is a strictly increasing sequence of positive integers such that the subsequences \n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578b37a84533d816f7bb21a83536aa751620abc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{s_1},s_{s_2},s_{s_3},\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943bd637535b539c3df40146ad44f3ab658db56c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{s_1+1},s_{s_2+1},s_{s_3+1},\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"13\" /> </center>\n<p>are both arithmetic progressions. Prove that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7dd022774271e03b3e6fa8e84093b89e1aec93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1,s_2,s_3,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"11\" /> is itself an arithmetic progression.\n</p><p><i>Author: Gabriel Carroll, USA</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4.\">Problem 4.</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4.\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99bbe74cccdc92b249d376f13d9429d41a8b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. The angle bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> meet the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the incentre of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9ad63616bd49b87f4b738bc90b17d6a77352d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEK=45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" />. Find all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><i>Authors: Jan Vonk and Peter Vandendriessche, Belgium, and Hojoo Lee, South Korea</i>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5.\">Problem 5.</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5.\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> from the set of positive integers to the set of positive integers such that, for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, there exists a non-degenerate triangle with sides of lengths \n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e645a0393a2bb5633d525e276321203781753af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e24db20845eba2e50f55b74a222d4ef4858c53a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b+f(a)-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. </center>\n<p>(A triangle is <i>non-degenerate</i> if its vertices are not collinear.) \n</p><p><i>Author: Bruno Le Floch, France</i>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6.\">Problem 6.</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6.\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b70976eb4ca80d39934c9d9dce6509ac4399208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> be distinct positive integers and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> positive integers not containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf1b314382b046f353617a43705a1f111de62ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=a_1+a_2+\\ldots+a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"13\" />. A grasshopper is to jump along the real axis, starting at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> jumps to the right with lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b70976eb4ca80d39934c9d9dce6509ac4399208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> in some order. Prove that the order can be chosen in such a way that the grasshopper never lands on any point in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><i>Author: Dmitry Khramtsov, Russia</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO\" title=\"2009 IMO\">2009 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems\">2008 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems\">2010 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018054054\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 295/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 854/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 74/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9251/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.608      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.608      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8306:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018054054 and revision id 133459. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}